<div class="unit-details">
    <div class="content-box">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i> MAIN TASK – Swipe Scenarios</h2>

        <p>Do you behave the same way on every app? In this activity, you will explore how online behaviour adapts and changes across different digital spaces. You'll be shown a series of scenario cards describing online situations and actions – your job is to swipe and sort them!</p>

        <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #eee; margin: 1.5rem 0;">

        <h3>How to Play</h3>
        <p>Each card describes a <strong>scenario</strong> (a situation) and an <strong>action</strong> (what someone did). 
        Read both sides of the card, then swipe it in the direction that best matches your judgement:</p>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
            <div style="background: #e8f5e9; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
                <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">←</span>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;"><strong>Good & Use Your Name</strong></p>
                <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666; margin: 0;">No need to hide who you are</p>
            </div>
            <div style="background: #fff3e0; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
                <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">→</span>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;"><strong>Good but Stay Anonymous</strong></p>
                <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666; margin: 0;">Better to use a nickname</p>
            </div>
            <div style="background: #e3f2fd; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
                <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">↑</span>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;"><strong>It Depends…</strong></p>
                <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666; margin: 0;">This one is complicated</p>
            </div>
            <div style="background: #ffebee; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
                <span style="font-size: 1.5rem;">↓</span>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;"><strong>Not OK Online</strong></p>
                <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666; margin: 0;">This shouldn't happen</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #eee; margin: 1.5rem 0;">

        <h3>Exercise Book Tasks</h3>
        <p>After completing the game, you'll write about your sorted cards in your exercise book:</p>

        <ul class="custom-list">
            <li><strong>From "Not OK Online":</strong> Choose one card and explain why this behaviour is never acceptable.</li>
            <li><strong>From "Good & Use Your Name":</strong> Choose one card and explain why being yourself is good in this situation.</li>
            <li><strong>From "Good but Stay Anonymous":</strong> Choose one card and explain why staying anonymous makes sense.</li>
            <li><strong>From "It Depends…":</strong> Choose 3-4 cards and explore what makes each one complicated.</li>
        </ul>

        <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #eee; margin: 1.5rem 0;">

        <h3>Reflection Questions</h3>

        <div style="background: #f8f9fa; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
            <h4 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--primary-color);">A. Adapting Your Behaviour</h4>
            <p style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Think about your sorted cards. Why do people behave differently on different platforms?</p>

            <h4 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--primary-color);">B. Context Collapse</h4>
            <p>What happens when something you post for your friends is suddenly seen by teachers, parents, or strangers? How does this change things?</p>
        </div>

        <div
            style="background: #eef2f7; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin: 2rem 0; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);">
            <h4 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--primary-color);"><i
                    class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap"></i> By the End of This Task, You Should Be Able To…</h4>
            <ul class="custom-list" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <li>Identify ways online behaviour changes across different platforms</li>
                <li>Explain how digital identity can evolve over time</li>
                <li>Recognise when behaviour needs to adapt for safety, privacy, or wellbeing</li>
                <li>Understand the concept of "context collapse" in online spaces</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

